<https://synbiohub.org/public/igem/BBa_R0062/1> <http://wiki.synbiohub.org/wiki/Terms/synbiohub#mutableDescription> "Promoter activated by LuxR in concert with HSL</p>   <p>The lux cassette of V. fischeri contains a left and a right promoter. The      right promoter gives weak constitutive expression of downstream genes.This      expression is up-regulated by the action of the LuxR activator protein complexed      with the autoinducer, 3-oxo-hexanoyl-HSL. Two molecules of LuxR protein form      a complex with two molecules of the signalling compound homoserine lactone      (HSL). This complex binds to a palindromic site on the promoter, increasing      the rate of transcription." .
